+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770003
+name: HMBS-related hepatic porphyria
+def: "A hepatic porphyria caused by monoallelic and biallelic variants in the HMBS gene and presenting as a spectrum of disease. Monoallelic variants predispose to acute or episodic attacks in adulthood with abdominal pain, neuropathy, and neuropsychiatric symptoms without cutaneous manifestations. Triggers precipitating acute attacks include estrogen or progesterone, oral contraceptives, alcohol, drugs, stress, or infections. Biallelic variants cause severe disease in childhood presenting with neurological issues including developmental abnormalities, ataxia, dysarthria, leukoencephalopathy, cataracts, and optic nerve hypoplasia." [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/, https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703]
+subset: clingen {source="MONDO:CLINGEN"}
+subset: rare
