+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770004
+name: PPOX-related hepatic porphyria
+def: "A hepatic porphyria caused by monoallelic and biallelic variants in the PPOX gene and presenting as a spectrum of disease. Cases caused by monoallelic variants may have onset during adolescence or adulthood and are episodic, characterized by abdominal pain, constipation, vomiting, muscular paralysis, and psychosis. Other symptoms may include abnormal blistering of the skin, cutaneous photosensitivity, and neuropathy. Triggers precipitating acute attacks include estrogen or progesterone, oral contraceptives, alcohol, drugs, stress, or infections. Cases caused by biallelic variants, which reduce enzyme activity to less than 25% of normal, typically result in child or adolescent onset with greater severity including brachydactyly, clinodactyly, intellectual disability, nystagmus, myopia, growth retardation, and hyperpigmentation." [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/, https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703]
+subset: clingen {source="MONDO:CLINGEN"}
+subset: rare
